## Final Judgement
## Summary of Key Insights

The evidence clearly establishes that Muhammadu Buhari was indeed the President of Nigeria on October 19, 2020. However, multiple official NNPC board member lists from both 2016 and 2020 do not include any daughter of Buhari. The only documented connection between Buhari's daughter (Zahra) and the petroleum sector is her appointment as "Deputy Manager" at the Petroleum Products Pricing Regulatory Agency (PPPRA), which is an NNPC-related entity but not the NNPC board itself. No credible news source or official government announcement confirms the appointment of any Buhari daughter to the NNPC board.

## Information Still Lacking

No further information is needed. The evidence is comprehensive and clear on this point.

## Conclusion

The claim is **refuted**. The evidence explicitly and clearly shows that no daughter of Muhammadu Buhari was ever appointed as a board member of the NNPC. The only documented appointment was Zahra Buhari's role as Deputy Manager at PPPRA (a separate regulatory agency), which is distinct from being a board member of NNPC. Multiple official board composition lists from 2016 and 2020 confirm that no Buhari daughter served on the NNPC board.

