### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim that a daughter of President Muhammadu Buhari served as a board member of the Nigerian National Petroleum Corporation (NNPC) is not supported by the evidence. While Buhari was indeed President on October 19, 2020, multiple official NNPC board composition lists from 2016 and 2020 ([BellaNaija, 2016](https://www.bellanaija.com/2016/07/president-buhari-appoints-new-nnpc-gmd-kachikwu-to-serve-as-board-chairman/); [The Whistler, 2020](https://thewhistler.ng/just-in-new-nnpc-board-inaugurated/)) include no family members of the President. The only documented connection is that Zahra Buhari was appointed as Deputy Manager at the Petroleum Products Pricing Regulatory Agency (PPPRA) ([Nairaland](https://www.nairaland.com/5679927/anger-buharis-daughter-made-manager)), a separate regulatory entity unrelated to the NNPC board. Official government announcements, such as the one reported by [Daily Nigerian](https://dailynigerian.com/buhari-appoints-late-chuba/), likewise list no Buhari daughter among NNPC board appointees, confirming the claim is false.